
/*
 * ============================================================
 * Scripting and Execution - QUICK REFERENCE GUIDE
 * ============================================================
 *
 * 1. LOCATING ELEMENTS USING BROWSER DEVELOPER TOOLS
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * Open browser Developer Tools (F12) and navigate to the
 * Elements tab to inspect and identify web elements.
 *
 * XPath Selector:
 * $x('//button[@name="add-to-cart-sauce-labs-backpack"]')
 * - Finds elements matching the specified XPath expression.
 *
 * CSS Selector:
 * $('button[name="add-to-cart-sauce-labs-backpack"]')
 * - Finds the first element matching the CSS selector.
 *
 * JavaScript DOM Selector:
 * document.querySelector('button[name="add-to-cart-sauce-labs-backpack"]')
 * - Returns the first matching element using JavaScript.
 *
 *
 * 2. RECORDING PLAYWRIGHT TESTS
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * npx playwright codegen https://www.saucedemo.com
 * - Launches Playwright Codegen to record browser interactions
 *   and automatically generate test scripts.
 *
 *
 * 3. EXECUTING PLAYWRIGHT TESTS
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * npx playwright test
 * - Executes all tests in headless mode by default.
 *
 * npx playwright test --headed
 * - Executes tests with the browser window visible.
 *
 * npx playwright test --ui
 * - Opens Playwright's interactive UI Mode for running,
 *   inspecting, and debugging tests.
 *
 * npx playwright test login.spec.js
 * - Executes only the tests in the login.spec.js file.
 *
 *
 * 4. DEBUGGING AND FILTERING TESTS
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * npx playwright test --debug
 * - Launches Playwright Inspector to debug tests step by step.
 *
 * npx playwright test --grep "@smoke"
 * - Executes only tests whose titles or tags match "@smoke".
 *
 *
 * 5. VIEWING TEST EXECUTION REPORTS
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * npx playwright show-report
 * - Opens the Playwright HTML report to review test results,
 *   execution details, screenshots, and traces when available.
 *
 * npx allure serve allure-results
 * - Generates and opens an Allure report from existing
 *   Allure test results (requires Allure CLI).
 *
 *
 * 6. RUNNING TESTS USING NPM SCRIPTS
 * ------------------------------------------------------------
 * npm test
 * - Executes the default test script defined in package.json.
 *
 * npm run test:headed
 * - Executes the custom test:headed script in package.json.
 *
 * npm run test:ui
 * - Executes the custom test:ui script in package.json.
 
 *
 * ============================================================
 */
